  "notes": "Composed of {打|だ} (to strike, to hit) + {電|でん} (electricity, telegram). The verb {打|う}つ was historically used for sending telegrams because telegraph operators physically tapped a key to transmit Morse code.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {打電|だでん}する: to send a telegram\n- {至急|しきゅう}{打電|だでん}: urgent telegram\n- {打電|だでん}を{受|う}ける: to receive a telegram\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {電報|でんぽう}: telegram — the general word for the message itself\n- {祝電|しゅくでん}: congratulatory telegram — a specific type\n- {弔電|ちょうでん}: condolence telegram — a specific type\n- {発電|はつでん}: in addition to its common meaning of \"power generation,\" can also mean sending a telegram (though this usage is rare)",
